From: Koral Ilgun <koral.ilgun@smartrg.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:55:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: clear RSNXE Used when the FT response omits the RSNXE

A non-AP STA that sends no RSNXE in its FT Reassociation Request,
for example one that uses SAE without H2E, gets a Reassociation
Response without the RSNXE. The AP still set the RSNXE Used subfield
of the FTE MIC Control field whenever sae_pwe is 1 or 2, so the
response announced an element that it did not carry and that the
MIC did not cover. hostapd discards a request with this combination.
Some STAs apply the same check to the response, discard it and send
the request again, so the FT protocol never completes for them.

Set RSNXE Used only when the response carries the RSNXE. A STA that
sent an RSNXE gets the same response as before.
---
 src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c |    7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
+++ b/src/ap/wpa_auth_ft.c
@@ -2714,7 +2714,12 @@ u8 * wpa_sm_write_assoc_resp_ies(struct
 		anonce = NULL;
 		snonce = NULL;
 	}
-	rsnxe_used = (auth_alg == WLAN_AUTH_FT) &&
+	/*
+	 * A response without the RSNXE must not announce one: some STAs
+	 * discard a response whose RSNXE Used bit and RSNXE do not match,
+	 * as hostapd discards such a request.
+	 */
+	rsnxe_used = (auth_alg == WLAN_AUTH_FT) && !omit_rsnxe &&
 		(conf->sae_pwe == SAE_PWE_HASH_TO_ELEMENT ||
 		 conf->sae_pwe == SAE_PWE_BOTH);
 #ifdef CONFIG_TESTING_OPTIONS
